{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>The Rock.</b> Unchanging — His hand is not too short to save, nor His ear too heavy to hear; and likewise no injustice can be attributed to Him, since you know from the signs that His deed in existence is perfect — to Him nothing can be added, and from Him nothing can be diminished." "And by this it is known <b>that all His ways are justice.</b> The ways of His goodness and the measure of His judgment are all justice, without doubt." "<b>El of faithfulness.</b> Faithful to what He swore to the fathers — to do good to the children on the merit of the fathers." "<b>And without injustice.</b> Even when He brings punishment." "<b>Righteous.</b> He loves righteousness, and by His righteousness He will not forsake His people." "<b>And upright is He.</b> In that He does not defraud any creature of its reward, and repays His enemies to their face — and therefore He extends Himself and does good to the nations in this world."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:55.253594978Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}